# MK-K68-LightSmart -- access to the 68-key board's vendor HID interface.
#
# The keyboard presents three HID interfaces. Only interface 2 (usage page
# 0xFF13) carries configuration traffic; interfaces 0 and 1 carry the keys
# you type. The DEVPATH match pins the rule to interface 2 so the typing
# interfaces are NOT handed to the session -- without it, any process
# running as the logged-in user could read raw keystrokes straight off the
# device. That matters doubly here: this keyboard reports Apple's
# 05ac:024f, so a broad rule would also expose a genuine Apple keyboard on
# the same machine.
#
# ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber} cannot be used alongside ATTRS{idVendor}: udev
# requires all ATTRS matches to land on the same parent device, and those
# two live on different ones. DEVPATH is an event key, so it composes.
# ":1.2" is bConfigurationValue 1, bInterfaceNumber 2.
#
# The file must sort before 70-uaccess.rules, hence the 60- prefix:
# uaccess is applied by a builtin that rule invokes, so a tag set later
# never takes effect.
#
# Install:  sudo cp 60-mk-k68-lightsmart.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#           sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#           sudo udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=hidraw
#
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="024f", DEVPATH=="*:1.2/*", TAG+="uaccess"
